   in terms of the fully relativistic spin-polarized screened {KKR} method},
   author    = {L Szunyogh and B \'Ujfalussy and P Weinberger},
   journal   = prb,
   year      = {1995},
   volume    = {51},
   pages     = {9552-9559},
   addendum  = {In order to treat the orientation of the magnetic field at surfaces
properly, the spin-polarized fully relativistic version of the screened
Korringa-Kohn-Rostoker method for semi-infinite systems is presented.
Magnetic anisotropy energies up to six iron layers on Au(001) are calculated
by using the force theorem, predicting a change from a perpendicular to a
parallel magnetization for a layer:
