   addendum  = {

"Compressed hydrogen is the oldest method for
hydrogen storage. Hydrogen tanks at 35 and 70 MPa is used for
on-board hydrogen storage [20e22]. Using this method, the
technology is simple and inexpensive. Limitations of this
method are due to the low volumetric density and the risk of
accidents. In case of an accident hydrogen is released instantaneously
over time, which significantly increases the risk of
explosion and is a huge minus for a safe operation."

"On the other hand one of the most important advantages of the storage
into activated carbon is that incase of anaccident hydrogen
is released not instantaneously (as for cryo-compression) but
gradually over time, which significantly reduces the risk of
explosion and is a huge plus for a safe operation."

   },
}

